<h2>I. Accreditation</h2>
<p>The Registry accredits the Registrar to provide registration services for TLDs operated by the Registry, subject to the Registry's published policies and this Agreement.</p>
<h2>II. Registrar Obligations</h2>
<p>The Registrar must comply with applicable law, relevant ICANN requirements where applicable, and Registry policies. The Registrar shall maintain secure and compatible technical systems, provide reliable customer support, and maintain effective abuse handling procedures.</p>
<h2>III. Registry Obligations</h2>
<p>The Registry will provide the Registrar access to its EPP and other registration systems and appropriate support, and will provide reasonable notice of material changes to policies and fees.</p>
<h2>IV. Financial Terms</h2>
<p>Registration, renewal, transfer, and other applicable fees are payable under the published Registry price schedule or any additional agreement between the parties.</p>
<h2>V. Intellectual Property</h2>
<p>All rights in the Registry, its registration systems, trademarks, and TLD administration remain with their respective owners. No ownership interest is transferred by accreditation.</p>
<h2>VI. Term and Termination</h2>
<p>Accreditation begins only upon Registry approval. The agreement remains in force until terminated as provided by applicable Registry policies and any separately negotiated accreditation terms.</p>
<h2>VII. Liability</h2>
<p>Applicable liability limitations and remedies are governed by law and the parties' applicable accreditation terms.</p>
<h2>VIII. Confidentiality</h2>
<p>The parties shall protect confidential information received in connection with the accreditation relationship in accordance with applicable law.</p>
<h2>IX. Dispute Resolution</h2>
<p>Disputes shall be resolved under the Registry's applicable accreditation policies and any separately agreed governing-law and dispute-resolution terms.</p>
<h2>X. General Provisions</h2>
<p>Any amendment must be agreed by the parties in writing. Each party confirms that the signatory has authority to execute this Agreement.</p>
